WEBVTT

01:23.650 --> 01:27.862
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:39.123 --> 01:40.416
Footsteps.

01:41.668 --> 01:43.211
What a surprise.

01:43.211 --> 01:44.879
They really are grilling meat.

01:46.005 --> 01:49.676
I hope they're not criminals or that sort
who aren't allowed back on the surface.

01:49.676 --> 01:51.427
We're just camping.

01:51.427 --> 01:53.429
We mean no harm.

01:54.889 --> 01:56.182
Wait a minute, I know that voice.

01:56.766 --> 01:58.017
Just as I thought!

01:58.017 --> 01:59.435
It's you, Laios!

01:59.435 --> 02:00.937
- Namari!
- Namari!

02:00.937 --> 02:02.230
You know them?

02:02.230 --> 02:03.690
They're my former party members.

02:03.690 --> 02:05.859
Hey, it's been a while.

02:05.859 --> 02:07.694
Well, I guess it's only been a week.

02:08.278 --> 02:09.863
Oh, let me introduce these people.

02:09.863 --> 02:13.366
These are my current employers,
Mr. and Mrs. Tansu.

02:13.950 --> 02:16.119
They work as someone's personal scholars,

02:16.119 --> 02:18.121
and they pay really well.

02:18.121 --> 02:20.623
And these two are the twins,
Kaka and Kiki.

02:21.207 --> 02:23.501
To be honest,
I can never remember who's who.

02:24.377 --> 02:27.130
Namari, how can you act like this

02:27.797 --> 02:30.008
after abandoning Falin?

02:30.008 --> 02:31.551
Abandon?

02:31.551 --> 02:35.513
I simply refused
to walk into the jaws of death for free.

02:36.556 --> 02:38.224
You...

02:39.100 --> 02:40.894
Marcille, take it easy.

02:40.894 --> 02:44.063
Hey, don't push yourselves.

02:44.063 --> 02:47.066
Falin wouldn't want
anything to happen to you.

02:47.901 --> 02:48.735
Right.

02:48.735 --> 02:50.904
Is there a healer in your party?

02:50.904 --> 02:52.614
My friend needs treatment.

02:52.614 --> 02:54.866
What do we get in return?

02:59.203 --> 03:00.455
We have Kelpie meat.

03:00.455 --> 03:01.372
No, thanks!

03:02.290 --> 03:03.249
Let's go, Namari.

03:03.249 --> 03:06.461
Handing out charity in a dungeon
just sets you up to be taken advantage of.

03:06.461 --> 03:09.631
Seriously, even that corpse
we stumbled upon on our way here

03:09.631 --> 03:11.257
had their own revival fee with them.

03:11.966 --> 03:13.760
Are you going to move on ahead?

03:13.760 --> 03:16.137
There's an Undine roaming around,
and it's dangerous.

03:16.137 --> 03:17.680
An Undine?

03:19.641 --> 03:21.726
So, this girl
angered a water spirit, did she?

03:23.728 --> 03:25.063
Don't underestimate us.

03:25.063 --> 03:29.317
We gnomes have been living alongside
gods and spirits since ancient times.

03:29.984 --> 03:35.531
To us, spirits are like neighbors,
not something to be afraid of.

03:38.117 --> 03:39.535
Undine!

03:39.535 --> 03:41.955
Oh, mighty water spirit!

03:41.955 --> 03:45.124
Heed my voice and respond to me!

03:45.875 --> 03:47.168
This isn't working.

03:50.004 --> 03:51.339
Grandpa Tansu!

03:59.722 --> 04:00.640
It didn't work.

04:00.640 --> 04:02.934
N-Namari!

04:02.934 --> 04:04.602
Namari died!

04:04.602 --> 04:06.145
She'll recover in no time.

04:06.145 --> 04:09.941
<i>Ira Fa Lane Brete Lane Bretego.</i>

04:13.736 --> 04:15.405
Damn you, you old geezer!

04:15.405 --> 04:17.782
You're always using me as your shield!

04:17.782 --> 04:20.868
That's why I compensate you handsomely!

04:20.868 --> 04:22.537
Resurrection magic, huh?

04:23.121 --> 04:25.999
It's a magic
I especially can't bring myself to like.

04:25.999 --> 04:28.418
You're against resurrection?

04:28.418 --> 04:31.421
It's not a pleasant sight to witness.

04:31.421 --> 04:34.465
It's unnatural for the dead
to come back to life.

04:34.465 --> 04:38.803
Outside the dungeon, sure,
but in here, it's normal.

04:38.803 --> 04:40.054
It's not normal.

04:40.638 --> 04:42.598
It's not normal, Laios.

04:42.598 --> 04:44.100
That's right.

04:44.684 --> 04:48.146
This dungeon
is under a very powerful enchantment.

04:49.230 --> 04:52.108
<i>It binds your soul to your body.</i>

04:52.108 --> 04:56.863
<i>So, no matter how damaged your body gets,
your soul is never released.</i>

04:56.863 --> 04:59.824
<i>And once your injuries are mended,
you can be revived.</i>

04:59.824 --> 05:01.659
In my perspective,

05:01.659 --> 05:04.704
this isn't the dead coming back to life.

05:04.704 --> 05:08.416
In this place, death itself is forbidden.

05:08.916 --> 05:12.128
It is a truly dreadful curse.

05:12.128 --> 05:13.838
But that aside,

05:14.422 --> 05:17.717
I study such ancient spells.

05:17.717 --> 05:21.095
I came here to investigate
a magic circle in this area,

05:21.721 --> 05:24.849
but as you can see,
my escort isn't very dependable.

05:26.934 --> 05:29.062
If you help me with my investigation,

05:29.062 --> 05:31.355
I will heal your companion.

05:37.612 --> 05:38.863
Deal.

05:38.863 --> 05:41.741
Senshi and I will accompany you.

05:47.747 --> 05:48.873
This should be the area.

05:50.208 --> 05:52.043
Elven characters.

05:52.043 --> 05:54.128
What terrible penmanship.

05:54.128 --> 05:56.214
The roots are in the way. Remove them.

06:00.343 --> 06:04.305
Laios, you still have that creepy sword?

06:04.889 --> 06:06.432
I keep telling you, but--

06:06.432 --> 06:08.768
"Use one from the shop," right? I know.

06:08.768 --> 06:10.603
You have to get one crafted by a dwarf.

06:10.603 --> 06:13.189
And avoid shops
that are tended by a half-foot.

06:13.189 --> 06:15.024
And don't use the same scabbard.

06:15.024 --> 06:15.942
And...

06:15.942 --> 06:19.028
You should give your weapon
some care now and then!

06:19.028 --> 06:20.613
I pity your axe!

06:22.406 --> 06:24.617
You probably think
I'm being annoying, don't you?

06:24.617 --> 06:25.576
No.

06:26.160 --> 06:29.789
When it comes to handling weapons,
I trust you more than anyone else.

06:39.841 --> 06:40.842
Stay back.

06:41.342 --> 06:42.385
What is it?

06:42.385 --> 06:43.594
There's a monster lurking.

06:43.594 --> 06:45.012
Then kill it.

06:45.012 --> 06:47.140
I don't know what or where it is.

06:47.807 --> 06:49.892
Then how can you be certain
there's a monster?

06:49.892 --> 06:51.310
J-Just a feeling.

06:51.310 --> 06:52.478
Are you serious?

06:52.478 --> 06:53.855
Mr. Tansu.

06:54.438 --> 06:57.608
You should trust Laios
when he's like this.

06:57.608 --> 07:00.653
I can't afford
to entertain a baseless suspicion.

07:00.653 --> 07:03.281
If it's lurking, simply drag it out.

07:17.044 --> 07:19.589
Oh, I see.

07:19.589 --> 07:21.424
It's a Tentacles.

07:21.424 --> 07:23.217
This isn't the time to admire it!

07:23.217 --> 07:25.761
Kiki! Hang in there!

07:25.761 --> 07:27.138
Hey, don't just stand there!

07:27.138 --> 07:29.015
Defeat the monster already!

07:29.015 --> 07:30.641
Our weapons can't reach it.

07:30.641 --> 07:32.393
Hurry up and do something!

07:32.977 --> 07:35.855
What if we purposefully let ourselves
get caught to get up close?

07:35.855 --> 07:38.149
Tentacles is part of the cnidarian family.

07:38.733 --> 07:40.443
<i>If their feelers
make contact with your skin,</i>

07:40.443 --> 07:42.653
<i>they shoot out venomous spines
that paralyze you.</i>

07:43.237 --> 07:46.157
If we get caught, there's a good chance
we won't make it out alive.

07:46.157 --> 07:48.284
Even if you die, I'll resurrect you!

07:48.284 --> 07:49.285
Listen...

07:49.285 --> 07:51.329
Fine. I'll go.

07:52.038 --> 07:54.790
Senshi, let me borrow your helmet.

07:58.085 --> 08:00.296
Laios, you shouldn't do this!

08:00.296 --> 08:03.257
You shouldn't count
on the success rate of resurrection magic.

08:03.257 --> 08:04.509
It's going to be okay.

08:05.092 --> 08:08.387
Because you and Senshi
are who I'm counting on.

08:10.473 --> 08:13.059
- Huh? What did he mean by that?
- I don't know.

08:13.059 --> 08:14.143
All right.

08:14.143 --> 08:16.395
Hey! Over here, Tentacles!

08:20.441 --> 08:21.817
Ow!

08:21.817 --> 08:24.320
They're piercing me through my armor,
just as I feared.

08:25.321 --> 08:27.823
My arms are already going numb.

08:28.324 --> 08:29.200
But...

08:29.784 --> 08:31.327
What on earth are you doing, Laios?

08:31.327 --> 08:32.536
Target its midsection!

08:32.536 --> 08:33.454
Its midsection!

08:45.800 --> 08:46.634
Dammit.

08:46.634 --> 08:47.718
<i>So that's what he meant!</i>

08:48.302 --> 08:51.013
<i>He gave me the trickiest task!</i>

08:58.104 --> 08:59.063
Kiki!

09:04.610 --> 09:06.612
Laios, are you okay?

09:09.490 --> 09:11.409
I guess not.

09:14.912 --> 09:16.831
Wait, what?

09:16.831 --> 09:19.375
Oh, Kiki. What happened to you?

09:19.375 --> 09:21.294
I'll heal you right away.

09:23.546 --> 09:25.464
This is going to be a little tricky.

09:25.464 --> 09:28.050
Sorry, this might take a while.

09:28.050 --> 09:29.427
Take your time.

09:30.052 --> 09:33.055
Is it just me,
or does your face look different?

09:33.055 --> 09:35.057
I got stung by a Tentacles.

09:35.558 --> 09:37.977
What should I do about this?

09:37.977 --> 09:40.062
Why are you grasping that?

09:40.062 --> 09:43.232
When I tore it off, my hand went numb,
and now I can't let go.

09:43.232 --> 09:45.651
Your hand looks like a gnome's now.

09:45.651 --> 09:46.986
Let me see.

09:47.570 --> 09:49.530
Ivy Tentacles, huh?

09:49.530 --> 09:52.742
"Rinsing it with vinegar can reduce
some of the stingers' activity."

09:52.742 --> 09:56.454
"It can have the opposite effect
depending on the species of Tentacles,

09:56.454 --> 09:57.496
so proceed with caution."

09:58.080 --> 10:01.500
"Make a cross-shaped incision
in the cross-section and peel vertically

10:01.500 --> 10:03.878
to remove the outer layer
with the stingers."

10:03.878 --> 10:07.882
TENTACLES WITH VINEGAR DRESSING

10:07.882 --> 10:09.800
Apparently, it tastes pretty good.

10:09.800 --> 10:10.926
Are you joking?

10:10.926 --> 10:13.512
No, it's just a fun fact...

10:13.512 --> 10:16.265
If that's the only way,
then I have no other choice.

10:16.265 --> 10:17.516
What?

10:18.184 --> 10:20.478
I see. It's not bad.

10:20.478 --> 10:23.230
If prepared right,
it'll be even more delicious.

10:23.230 --> 10:24.649
Let me have a bite, too!

10:26.692 --> 10:27.902
This...

10:27.902 --> 10:30.696
tastes different depending on the part!

10:30.696 --> 10:32.406
You're definitely imagining it.

10:32.406 --> 10:34.116
No, it's true!

10:34.116 --> 10:35.159
Try it.

10:37.703 --> 10:39.914
It only tastes like vinegar.

10:40.498 --> 10:42.208
Do you want a bite, too, Marcille?

10:42.208 --> 10:43.876
Huh? What is it?

10:45.795 --> 10:47.213
It tastes sour.

10:47.213 --> 10:49.256
It's kinda gooey.

10:49.757 --> 10:52.676
- It's taro root. Tell me it's taro root.
- You, too, Namari.

10:52.676 --> 10:55.096
This part. I recommend this part.

10:55.096 --> 10:56.722
No! No, thanks!

10:56.722 --> 10:59.433
We're not lacking food!

11:00.017 --> 11:01.310
It tastes good, though.

11:01.310 --> 11:04.188
Not quite,
but it could be if prepared right.

11:04.188 --> 11:06.982
Either stew it or mash it and then fry it.

11:06.982 --> 11:08.442
Sounds good!

11:10.027 --> 11:11.362
It slipped off!

11:15.116 --> 11:16.325
Sorry for the wait.

11:16.325 --> 11:17.910
I'll treat you now.

11:17.910 --> 11:19.328
Thank you.

11:19.328 --> 11:21.956
Well then, please heal her first.

11:24.583 --> 11:31.465
<i>Ilava Rietge Atheus Pilitos
Nuswera Iboiseme Seus Wehrba.</i>

11:35.386 --> 11:38.681
It feels awesome being in good health!

11:39.723 --> 11:42.059
Thank you, Mr. Tansu.

11:42.059 --> 11:42.977
You, too, Laios.

11:43.894 --> 11:45.354
What's with your face?

11:45.354 --> 11:46.856
Thank Namari instead.

11:46.856 --> 11:47.773
What?

11:48.315 --> 11:51.068
Your marksmanship was truly remarkable.

11:51.068 --> 11:53.279
It's amazing you took it down
with just one shot.

11:53.279 --> 11:56.574
We're lucky you're skilled
with a crossbow, too.

11:56.574 --> 11:59.618
Actually, it was my first time using one.

11:59.618 --> 12:00.536
What?

12:01.162 --> 12:02.204
Namari.

12:03.456 --> 12:06.876
Thanks for giving us a hand.

12:06.876 --> 12:08.878
I'll set aside the incident
with Falin for now.

12:08.878 --> 12:11.213
You're most welcome.

12:11.213 --> 12:16.010
Getting paid makes you give it your best,
more so than doing it for free.

12:19.763 --> 12:21.390
Now, now, you two.

12:21.390 --> 12:22.933
It's all in the past now.

12:22.933 --> 12:24.560
It totally isn't!

12:24.560 --> 12:28.314
Why are you, of all people,
acting like it's none of your business?

12:28.314 --> 12:29.690
Unbelievable!

12:29.690 --> 12:31.901
- That's not what I meant!
- Are you the leader?

12:31.901 --> 12:33.486
Tough role, huh?

12:36.739 --> 12:38.282
It's looking this way.

12:39.158 --> 12:40.951
Is it still upset?

12:40.951 --> 12:44.663
What did you do
to make the spirit so furious?

12:44.663 --> 12:47.082
I've never been attacked by one
so fiercely before.

12:47.082 --> 12:50.628
I may have accidentally poured
boiling water directly onto it.

12:50.628 --> 12:53.797
That's not good. Typical of an elf.

12:53.797 --> 12:55.466
Elves...

12:55.466 --> 12:57.843
My race has nothing to do with it!

12:58.427 --> 13:02.223
Is there a way to pacify the spirit
without using magic?

13:02.223 --> 13:03.599
That's simple.

13:03.599 --> 13:06.977
<i>An Undine is a collective of tiny spirits.</i>

13:06.977 --> 13:10.272
<i>If the individuals comprising it
naturally dies off,</i>

13:10.272 --> 13:13.359
<i>their hostility will fade away
as new generations emerge.</i>

13:13.359 --> 13:17.530
The lifespan of a spirit
is a week at most.

13:17.530 --> 13:19.365
A week?

13:20.157 --> 13:21.784
I can't wait that long.

13:21.784 --> 13:23.369
Neither can we.

13:23.369 --> 13:26.997
So, we will return to the surface for now.

13:26.997 --> 13:29.833
We'll resume our investigation
another time.

13:29.833 --> 13:32.461
Hey, let's prepare the return spell.

13:33.462 --> 13:36.382
Hey, Laios.
They're preparing the return spell.

13:37.716 --> 13:39.969
Mr. Tansu, I have a favor to ask you.

13:41.971 --> 13:44.515
You want me to return
to the surface with them?

13:44.515 --> 13:46.809
Now? After coming all this way?

13:46.809 --> 13:49.144
You're currently out of magic.

13:49.144 --> 13:52.273
I've heard that running out of magic
is similar to having anemia.

13:52.856 --> 13:55.192
You should head back to the surface
with Mr. Tansu's party.

13:55.192 --> 13:56.443
I'm fine.

13:56.443 --> 13:58.529
I'm actually quite surprised
by how great I feel.

13:58.529 --> 14:00.239
Oh, I think it might be due to the liver.

14:00.239 --> 14:03.409
Eating nutritious food won't result
in immediate changes to your condition.

14:03.409 --> 14:05.369
- It's one's daily--
- I'll listen to that later.

14:05.369 --> 14:07.830
I really feel fantastic.

14:07.830 --> 14:10.457
I think some of my magic returned as well
after a short rest.

14:10.457 --> 14:15.296
But your staff doesn't seem
to have the usual magical aura.

14:15.296 --> 14:17.590
T-That's because...

14:20.342 --> 14:21.552
Let's leave her.

14:22.553 --> 14:24.138
Why are you laughing?

14:24.138 --> 14:27.558
It's just that I've never seen you
with that expression before.

14:28.142 --> 14:29.059
But...

14:29.059 --> 14:31.478
what are you going to do
when you're on your own?

14:31.478 --> 14:34.273
The three of you
can't fight a dragon by yourselves.

14:34.273 --> 14:36.066
Don't count me in.

14:36.066 --> 14:41.780
Plus, that axe of yours doesn't seem like
it could harm a dragon in the slightest.

14:43.449 --> 14:47.328
Namari, you've defeated
many dragons, right?

14:48.370 --> 14:49.204
Yeah.

14:49.788 --> 14:51.707
Well then...

14:54.168 --> 14:55.461
Please, Namari.

14:55.461 --> 14:57.087
Rejoin our party!

14:57.671 --> 14:58.964
Are you serious?

14:58.964 --> 15:02.593
Help Laios' party defeat the Red Dragon.

15:02.593 --> 15:05.054
I want to rescue Falin, no matter what!

15:05.554 --> 15:06.930
Just this once!

15:06.930 --> 15:09.058
I'll find a way to gather the funds!

15:09.058 --> 15:10.768
Forget it, Marcille.

15:11.268 --> 15:12.603
Why?

15:12.603 --> 15:15.064
The adventurer community is small.

15:15.064 --> 15:17.775
Gossip travels like wildfire.

15:17.775 --> 15:21.362
Namari has been having
financial problems for some time now.

15:21.362 --> 15:24.448
And you got wind of it,
didn't you, Mr. Tansu?

15:24.448 --> 15:25.407
I did.

15:26.075 --> 15:28.994
Now, imagine if she rejoined
her former party for money.

15:29.578 --> 15:32.247
<i>"She'll do anything for the right price."</i>

15:32.247 --> 15:34.875
<i>That's what people will say about her.</i>

15:34.875 --> 15:38.253
<i>It may open up more job opportunities,</i>

15:38.253 --> 15:40.506
<i>but it'd probably attract
a different clientele.</i>

15:40.506 --> 15:42.424
So, forget it.

15:42.424 --> 15:44.885
Especially if you care
about both your futures.

15:46.095 --> 15:47.721
That's how it is.

15:47.721 --> 15:49.515
Forget it, Marcille.

15:57.523 --> 16:00.776
No. There's still another way.

16:00.776 --> 16:03.529
There's another way for me
to regain my magic.

16:03.529 --> 16:05.531
W-What is it?

16:06.240 --> 16:07.408
I drink...

16:08.075 --> 16:09.284
the Undine!

16:10.869 --> 16:12.746
What? The Undine?

16:13.664 --> 16:15.249
What's with your reactions?

16:15.249 --> 16:16.917
Where's your usual enthusiasm?

16:16.917 --> 16:18.919
I'm not so interested in spirits.

16:19.545 --> 16:21.880
Spirits live on magic.

16:21.880 --> 16:24.925
I'm certain they're abundant
in magical energy!

16:25.634 --> 16:29.096
<i>Capturing it seems trickier
than defeating it, though.</i>

16:29.096 --> 16:34.101
But water spirits are vulnerable to heat,
so maybe I can use that.

16:34.101 --> 16:36.770
Maybe we can attack it
with a heated weapon.

16:37.688 --> 16:41.900
Or maybe we can pour oil on the lake,
set it on fire, and trap the spirit?

16:43.485 --> 16:46.447
When it attacks, it spills on the ground,

16:46.447 --> 16:48.115
and maybe I could quickly drink that.

16:49.199 --> 16:52.494
It'd probably poke holes
in your body from the inside.

16:52.494 --> 16:53.746
You're right.

16:54.705 --> 16:56.373
Come on, think.

16:56.373 --> 16:57.499
There must be a way.

17:01.962 --> 17:04.298
By heating this pot
and using it as a shield,

17:04.298 --> 17:06.008
I could defend and attack simultaneously.

17:06.008 --> 17:08.594
Undines are powerful enough
to penetrate a stone column, though.

17:08.594 --> 17:10.637
You think that shabby pot can protect you?

17:10.637 --> 17:13.140
It's unfair to call it a shabby pot.

17:13.724 --> 17:16.769
It's a family heirloom that's been
passed down through generations.

17:16.769 --> 17:19.146
I have diligently maintained it.

17:19.146 --> 17:22.066
It never gets burnt
and it distributes heat evenly.

17:22.066 --> 17:23.650
It's an exceptional pot.

17:24.234 --> 17:25.402
Hold on.

17:27.237 --> 17:29.156
The color, the sheen,

17:29.740 --> 17:32.326
the weight, the texture...

17:32.326 --> 17:34.411
This is adamant!

17:34.411 --> 17:35.871
Unbelievable.

17:35.871 --> 17:37.915
As a weapon,
it can shatter a dragon's bone.

17:37.915 --> 17:39.958
As armor,
it shields even against a dragon's fangs.

17:39.958 --> 17:44.421
Adamant, the metal
that every blacksmith dreams of.

17:44.421 --> 17:46.423
So, why is it used for a pot?

17:46.423 --> 17:50.094
It was originally a shield,
but I had no need for it, so...

17:50.094 --> 17:52.054
How can you be so wasteful?!

17:52.054 --> 17:54.306
Do you think it could withstand
an Undine's assault?

17:54.306 --> 17:55.599
Of course, it could!

17:55.599 --> 17:57.976
We happen to have both a pot and a lid,

17:57.976 --> 18:00.729
so two of us can wield one each
to attack it from both sides...

18:01.313 --> 18:03.816
And we'll burn it with fire!

18:03.816 --> 18:05.609
It's the only option we have.

18:07.027 --> 18:07.861
<i>Really?</i>

18:07.861 --> 18:10.948
<i>Even if they have tough shields,
the Undine is so powerful.</i>

18:11.532 --> 18:15.661
<i>Maybe the dwarf could restrain it,
but is Laios strong enough?</i>

18:20.791 --> 18:22.876
Brace yourself as soon
as the surface starts to warp.

18:24.419 --> 18:26.338
Let's not waste this opportunity.

18:29.675 --> 18:30.968
Here comes!

18:32.803 --> 18:33.929
Laios!

18:42.271 --> 18:43.689
<i>What incredible power!</i>

18:51.405 --> 18:52.698
Laios!

19:02.958 --> 19:04.585
Namari...

19:16.972 --> 19:17.806
Now!

19:26.023 --> 19:27.816
Good. Keep going.

19:27.816 --> 19:29.443
Hang in there!

19:29.443 --> 19:31.320
Place it over the flames!

19:54.384 --> 19:56.094
So hot!

19:56.094 --> 19:58.513
- Wow, this is amazing!
- Incredible.

19:58.513 --> 20:00.474
What astounding strength!

20:01.058 --> 20:04.019
Namari, Senshi, thank you so much!

20:04.603 --> 20:05.729
You, too, Laios.

20:06.271 --> 20:07.314
Are you okay?

20:07.314 --> 20:09.650
Despite his physique, he's pretty flimsy.

20:09.650 --> 20:11.276
Just like a typical tall-man.

20:11.860 --> 20:12.861
Right.

20:21.411 --> 20:23.580
No need to drink it all in one go.

20:24.206 --> 20:27.042
Spirit magic is hard to absorb.

20:27.751 --> 20:32.798
It's fundamental to pair nutrition
with something that aids in absorption.

20:33.382 --> 20:34.549
Senshi.

20:35.259 --> 20:37.010
Let's start cooking.

20:38.387 --> 20:42.933
<i>Peel the potatoes, carrots,
onions, and the Tentacles.</i>

20:43.517 --> 20:45.018
<i>Then cut them into bite-sized pieces.</i>

20:46.186 --> 20:48.563
<i>Marinate the Kelpie meat
with salt and pepper,</i>

20:48.563 --> 20:50.774
<i>and fry until the surface changes color.</i>

20:50.774 --> 20:53.568
<i>Add the onions and carrots
and sauté them together,</i>

20:53.568 --> 20:55.612
<i>then put them into the Undine.</i>

20:57.906 --> 20:59.324
<i>Skim well,</i>

20:59.324 --> 21:02.953
<i>then add the potatoes
and spices and simmer.</i>

21:11.420 --> 21:12.796
It's done!

21:12.796 --> 21:15.340
UNDINE STEW WITH TENTACLES AND KELPIE

21:15.340 --> 21:17.259
Huh? Where did everyone go?

21:17.259 --> 21:20.220
They went to continue their investigation
at the tower across the water.

21:21.013 --> 21:22.431
We're back!

21:22.431 --> 21:24.850
I had no idea there would be so many.

21:24.850 --> 21:27.060
Good thing we dealt with them.

21:27.561 --> 21:29.104
H-Hey!

21:30.314 --> 21:33.108
Would you like to join us for a meal?

21:37.821 --> 21:39.072
Here you go.

21:39.573 --> 21:41.241
Looks good.

21:41.241 --> 21:43.285
Did you make this, Marcille?

21:43.285 --> 21:45.996
Senshi helped a lot.

21:46.747 --> 21:48.415
Here, Namari.

21:50.584 --> 21:53.170
You should start eating
instead of serving everyone.

21:53.170 --> 21:54.755
O-Okay.

22:08.143 --> 22:09.019
Yes!

22:09.019 --> 22:11.146
Some magic is starting to come back.

22:12.189 --> 22:13.231
You guys,

22:14.232 --> 22:17.069
did you come this far
while scavenging all this time?

22:17.069 --> 22:18.403
Yup.

22:18.987 --> 22:22.449
<i>I was ready to face criticism
for leaving the party,</i>

22:22.449 --> 22:25.577
<i>but I never expected
to see them resort to this.</i>

22:26.745 --> 22:29.164
<i>Maybe this is a form of punishment.</i>

22:35.504 --> 22:38.548
<i>It's delicious! The broth
has been infused into the ingredients.</i>

22:38.548 --> 22:40.717
<i>How did everything cook so quickly?</i>

22:40.717 --> 22:42.052
<i>Is it because of the pot?</i>

22:42.052 --> 22:44.638
<i>Could adamant
be a good material for making pots?</i>

22:45.222 --> 22:47.265
Senshi, was it?

22:47.766 --> 22:50.268
Um, about your axe...

22:50.936 --> 22:52.395
I apologize for making fun of it.

22:54.022 --> 22:55.148
It's all right.

22:55.148 --> 22:59.277
The truth is, I have no interest
in any blacksmithing work.

23:00.570 --> 23:02.739
I can't distinguish
different types of ore,

23:02.739 --> 23:06.451
and my old friends
used to get frustrated with me often.

23:08.161 --> 23:10.997
Namari, we're heading back to the surface.

23:12.541 --> 23:14.960
But you can stay here.

23:16.920 --> 23:18.463
What are you talking about?

23:18.463 --> 23:20.757
Try a bite at least!

23:20.757 --> 23:23.218
The texture is a bit odd,
but it tastes quite good!

23:23.218 --> 23:24.386
But...

23:24.386 --> 23:27.180
I know I can't ask you to trust me...

23:28.306 --> 23:30.767
but I want to be more
than just a hired hand.

23:30.767 --> 23:33.436
I want to be accepted as one of you.

23:34.563 --> 23:36.064
I'll work hard.

23:47.701 --> 23:50.453
Frankly, Chilchuck,

23:50.453 --> 23:53.123
I thought you'd be the first one
to leave the party.

23:53.123 --> 23:56.501
You're not the kind to accept unpaid work.

23:57.085 --> 23:57.919
Damn right.

23:57.919 --> 24:00.505
That's why I always insist
on getting paid upfront.

24:00.505 --> 24:04.759
But the problem is that I can't walk away
when situations like this arise.

24:04.759 --> 24:07.387
What? You stayed because it was your job?

24:07.387 --> 24:09.598
Not for your friends or friendship?

24:10.307 --> 24:11.641
Listen, Marcille.

24:11.641 --> 24:13.643
Let me tell you something important.

24:14.227 --> 24:16.521
Folks who claim
they don't need anything in return

24:16.521 --> 24:19.441
are the least trustworthy in this world.

24:20.609 --> 24:22.777
By the way, what's Shuro up to now?

24:23.361 --> 24:24.446
No idea.

24:24.446 --> 24:26.531
He seemed to have
another contact to reach out to.

24:26.531 --> 24:29.576
But he was so in love with Falin
that he wanted to propose to her.

24:29.576 --> 24:32.037
So, he's probably still
desperately searching for her.

24:32.787 --> 24:34.831
What? I had no clue.

24:34.831 --> 24:36.541
- He's so oblivious.
- Totally.

24:36.541 --> 24:38.543
Look, I get that you guys

24:39.127 --> 24:44.174
all care about Falin, but be sure
to make it back to the surface, okay?

24:46.676 --> 24:48.470
Namari, you take care, too.

24:56.519 --> 24:57.604
See ya!

26:27.819 --> 26:31.990
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
